  "sort": 0,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You conjure a floating, ghostly black lantern that hovers above you and sheds Dim Light in a 60-foot radius. When an enemy dies within this Dim Light, a fragment of its soul flies into the lantern. The lantern can hold a number of soul fragments equal to your spellcasting ability modifier, and they dissipate when the spell ends.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you can expend a soul fragment to create one of the following effects.</p><p><strong>Drain Life.</strong> The fragment darts at a creature of your choice that you can see within 60 feet of yourself. The target makes a Constitution saving throw, taking Necrotic damage equal to 4d8 plus your spellcasting ability modifier on a failure or half as much on a success.</p><p><strong>Repair Undead.</strong> The fragment flies into an Undead of your choice that you can see within 60 feet of yourself, which regains Hit Points equal to 4d8 plus your spellcasting ability modifier.</p><p><strong>Ward Ally.</strong> The fragment circles a creature of your choice that you can see within 60 feet of yourself. Other creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against it until the start of your next turn.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-viitn2XGuRreAwXI\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Count the soul fragments by hand.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
